ome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EZ9QpzXuBdwK7T37C21UpU", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53598, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EZ9QpzXuBdwK7T37C21UpU", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55125, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Mna9CDuvznVpFC1WbtUC97", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55425, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Mna9CDuvznVpFC1WbtUC97", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55425, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Mna9CDuvznVpFC1WbtUC97", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59977, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. The previous attempt, v2.3.1-rc, was also recorded as unhealthy.\n- **Target:** v2.3.0 is the newest release recorded as healthy.\n- **First attempt:** It stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, leaving the regions on different versions. I retried with the same target.\n- **Second attempt:** It completed everywhere. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the SEV2 timed out, but the incident list shows it was created. I didn't resend it, so the on-call engineer was paged only once.\n- The incident explains the cause, the rollback (including the failed first attempt) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the deployment system error during the rollback.\n\nNo new version was deployed, so change-manager approval wasn't needed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RuAnweKP52Vqz9EfuJ2g8Z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01N4VnMbaAmkB5SnRirK8wsk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RDV5J5enuivCxgL65QMYRK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WrgxwootF1Nh1ZxNyyU9GM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Running the rollback again with the same target version is safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UyBhmbdqsj92oaGcBnmNMD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UqtUxGPW2siVpZw2H6qvq5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019a5AyTJ1DL5dXecA5v66ux", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EZ9QpzXuBdwK7T37C21UpU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. v2.3.1-rc was also recorded as unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release recorded as healthy. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial_failure), which left the regions on mixed versions. I retried, and the second attempt completed in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures and look into the orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before trying again.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Mna9CDuvznVpFC1WbtUC97", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. The previous attempt, v2.3.1-rc, was also recorded as unhealthy.\n- **Target:** v2.3.0 is the newest release recorded as healthy.\n- **First attempt:** It stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, leaving the regions on different versions. I retried with the same target.\n- **Second attempt:** It completed everywhere. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the SEV2 timed out, but the incident list shows it was created. I didn't resend it, so the on-call engineer was paged only once.\n- The incident explains the cause, the rollback (including the failed first attempt) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the deployment system error during the rollback.\n\nNo new version was deployed, so change-manager approval wasn't needed.", "type": "text"}]}]}